Ghostty: allow trimming blank rows occupied only by a saved cursor

Applies after the libghostty-spm patch stack to Ghostty
0538f7535be0cbca6bbe54e6fde654d5c628f1f2.

A saved cursor below the live cursor must not prevent a height reduction
from trimming unused rows. Otherwise the live cursor can move into
scrollback, be clamped to row zero, and leave a duplicate prompt separated
by blank rows when the shell redraws after SIGWINCH.

Apply this patch when rebuilding the native Ghostty XCFramework. qmux
selects the resulting binary through the Package.swift override in
libghostty-spm-qmux.patch.

diff --git a/src/terminal/PageList.zig b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
--- a/src/terminal/PageList.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
@@ -1234,6 +1234,10 @@
     /// resize/reflow behavior depends on the cursor position.
     cursor: ?Cursor = null,

+    /// A tracked saved cursor follows reflow, but must not keep trailing blank
+    /// rows alive. If its row is trimmed, clamp it to the last retained row.
+    saved_cursor: ?*Pin = null,
+
     /// Whether the resize may pull rows out of scrollback back into the
     /// active area. If false, growing rows always appends blank rows at the
     /// bottom and a column reflow keeps the top of the active area on the
@@ -2873,7 +2877,7 @@
                 // behavior because it seemed fine in an ocean of differing behavior
                 // between terminal apps. I'm completely open to changing it as long
                 // as resize behavior isn't regressed in a user-hostile way.
-                const trimmed = self.trimTrailingBlankRows(self.rows - rows);
+                const trimmed = self.trimTrailingBlankRows(self.rows - rows, opts.saved_cursor);

                 // Account for our trimmed rows in the total row cache
                 self.total_rows -= trimmed;
@@ -3202,6 +3206,7 @@
 fn trimTrailingBlankRows(
     self: *PageList,
     max: size.CellCountInt,
+    saved_cursor: ?*Pin,
 ) size.CellCountInt {
     var trimmed: size.CellCountInt = 0;
     var invalidated_node: ?*List.Node = null;
@@ -3218,9 +3223,19 @@
         // we'd invalidate this pin, as well.
         const pin_keys = self.tracked_pins.keys();
         for (pin_keys) |p| {
+            if (p == saved_cursor) continue;
             if (p.node != row_pin.node or
                 p.y != row_pin.y) continue;
             return trimmed;
+        }
+
+        // The saved cursor is a restorable position, not live content. Move
+        // it before retiring this row, including when that frees its page.
+        // The active cursor and all other tracked pins still prevent trimming.
+        if (saved_cursor) |p| {
+            if (p.node == row_pin.node and p.y == row_pin.y) {
+                p.* = p.up(1).?;
+            }
         }

         // No text, we can trim this row. Because it has
